          <h2>When to Resurface Your Court</h2>
          <p>Court resurfacing is a cost-effective way to restore playing surfaces that have deteriorated due to weather, age, or heavy use. Rather than complete replacement, professional resurfacing can add years of life to your court at a fraction of the cost of new construction.</p>
          <p>Utah's diverse climate conditions — from freeze-thaw cycles in mountain areas to intense UV exposure in desert regions — can take a toll on court surfaces. Recognizing the signs that indicate resurfacing needs can help you maintain optimal playing conditions and prevent more extensive damage.</p>
