      <h2 class="text-center section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-section">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How long does resurfacing last compared to new construction?</h3>
          <p>Professional resurfacing typically lasts 5-8 years with proper maintenance, providing excellent value compared to new construction. The lifespan depends on usage, maintenance, and climate conditions, but resurfacing can extend total court life significantly.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Can you change court colors during resurfacing?</h3>
          <p>Absolutely! Resurfacing is the perfect time to update your court's color scheme. We can completely change colors, add multi-sport line systems, or incorporate custom designs and logos into the new surface.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How much does resurfacing cost compared to new court construction?</h3>
          <p>Resurfacing typically costs 30-50% less than new construction, making it an excellent value for courts with sound structural foundations. The exact savings depend on the extent of repairs needed and surface system selected.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Can you resurface in winter?</h3>
          <p>Utah winters present challenges for resurfacing due to temperature and moisture conditions. We typically recommend spring through fall for optimal results, though mild winter days may allow for certain types of repair work.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How soon can I play on the resurfaced court?</h3>
          <p>Most acrylic systems require 48-72 hours of cure time before light foot traffic, with full play recommended after 5-7 days. Weather conditions affect curing time, and we provide specific recommendations for each project.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

